=== 1. a bare clone plus a worktree: no checkout is the sole writer ===

$ git clone --bare source roadmap.git && git -C roadmap.git worktree add ../checkout HEAD
  Preparing worktree (detached HEAD ea55bf6)
  HEAD is now at ea55bf6 roadmap

$ git -C roadmap.git worktree list --porcelain | head -3
  worktree /tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/roadmap.git
  bare
  

…/checkout $ stepstone project list --cwd /tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/checkout
[open] ship-the-worktree-guard: Ship the worktree guard
[exit 0]

…/checkout $ stepstone project add Would fork the roadmap --cwd /tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/checkout --json
{
  "ok": false,
  "scope": "project",
  "action": "add",
  "error": {
    "code": "UNAVAILABLE",
    "message": "Project worklist /tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/checkout/.worklist/worklist.json cannot be changed from /tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/checkout: the repository at /tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/roadmap.git has no main worktree, so no checkout of it is the roadmap's sole writer. Restore the main worktree if it was removed, or make this change in a clone that has one; a store outside the committed roadmap paths, named by $STEPSTONE_WORKLIST, stays writable here.",
    "retryable": false,
    "details": {
      "path": "/tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/checkout/.worklist/worklist.json",
      "currentWorktree": "/tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/checkout",
      "gitDirectory": "/tmp/stepstone-r3/bare/roadmap.git",
      "resolution": "provide-main-worktree"
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "changed": false,
    "semanticNoOp": false,
    "changedFields": [],
    "cliVersion": "0.9.3"
  }
}
[exit 1]

the way out it names, taken from this very checkout:
